# The Status tab as cards.
#
# It used to be eighteen label/value lines on the bare ground, in one column, with a half-line
# of space every so often standing in for a grouping. Three cards say the grouping outright, and
# each one reports on itself in its own heading colour - so this clip is about the headings as
# much as the panels: watch "Radio" go from the accent to the bad tone as the firmware starts
# refusing packets, without a single row having to be read.

scene demo
config
tab status
hold 900

# The radio comes under pressure. Each of these is a row that only exists while something is
# wrong, which is why this card is the one that can outgrow the panel - and why it is ordered
# most-read first, so what fb_draw_card() drops is the free-heap figure and not the battery.
queue 6 16
hold 700
notice warn Duty cycle limit reached, transmit paused
hold 900
queue 0 16 refused
hold 900
reboots 2
hold 1000

# The same three cards in every theme. The fill is a role (SURFACE), the hairline is a role
# (RULE) and the heading is a tone, so nothing here is switched by hand - and on the contrast
# theme, where the surface is all but the ground, the hairline is the whole of the card.
theme light
hold 1000
theme contrast
hold 1000
theme colorblind
hold 1400
